这个她就越看唐小虾越顺眼，心想也不知道这个帅哥是聪明还是财迷，在这样匆忙的特殊环境下，居然还能想到先搞点钱再说！另一边唐小虾收好钱后已经缓缓的把凌云剑抽了出来，出鞘后的凌云剑微微泛着蓝光，一看就不是伍绪腰间那种凡品能比的。洛思琪的披雪剑剑身与剑鞘一样都是银白色的，银白色的光让她觉得有些冷，便赶忙把剑插了回去。清元子将两人送到了外面等候的伍家人面前，小师弟早已指挥侍女们把两人要用其他的东西用行囊收拾好，洛思琪也不知道小师弟都往行囊里给她收拾了什么，不过洛思琦觉得这都无所谓啦！反正她也不知道自己要收拾什么！伍绪对他们行了个礼，也没介绍伍家的其他人，对唐小虾和洛思琦说：“情况紧急，两位请跟我走吧！”伍绪和唐小虾差不多高，年龄大约有三十多岁的样子，洛思琪也没心思考虑他，转而去看小师弟牵来的那两匹马。小师弟牵来的马样子都很不错，不过这却是出给洛思琪的一个难题。来自现代社会的洛思琪根本是不会骑马的啊！洛思琪看了一下唐小虾，只见他也是面色凝重，不过他还是走到一匹大红马面前踩着上马石翻身骑了上去。洛思琦见他上马后差点歪下来，可还是抓住了马鬃强装镇定，他的脸看起来很苍白，可还是笑着对洛思琪喊道：“师妹，上来啊！和师哥同骑一匹马！”看着唐小虾刚才踏过的上马石，洛思琪狠了狠心就坐到了唐小虾的身后。这是洛思琪第一次骑真的马，她有些害怕。可又不好意思去抱唐小虾的腰，她甚至觉得唐小虾也是自身难保的，她害怕一会儿马真跑起来的话，自己抱住他只会让两个人通通摔到地上。因为有伍家的人在场唐小虾并没有对清元子说：“老头！再见！”而是说了一句，“师父，我们走了！”，便也拍马跟在伍家人的后面。马跑起来后有些颠簸，洛思琦为了不掉下去，也顾不得不好意思了，她轻轻的抱住了唐小虾的腰，唐小虾被她这一抱有些反应，微微伏低了身紧紧的抓住了马，才让两个人没有瞬间摔下来。因为出谷的路有很多弯路并且崎岖，所以两人骑马的速度其实并不快，待到洛思琪慢慢适应了在马背上的感觉，两人跟着伍家的马队也快出谷了。此时洛思琪忽然想起她和唐小虾在谷中住了许多天居然忘问清元子这山谷的名字了，她把这事和唐小虾一说，唐小虾不好意思的一笑说：“我也忘了！”不过待到谷口的时候，两人却看到了左侧的一处峭壁上用不知用什么刻出的三个用墨涂过的黑字，雪云谷！洛思琪不禁笑道：“这谷的名字真搞笑，这谷中花开遍地，绿草茵茵，哪里和雪沾得上边！要我看应该叫百花谷更合适！”唐小虾也赞同洛思琪的说法，他边驾着马边说：“是啊！雪云谷这名字一听就像在昆仑山那样的高海拔山脉中的峡谷，此地如果在楚国，那应该是长江中下游，这里的气候要下雪可是太难了！”出谷后，前面伍家的马队开始加快速度了，洛思琦在马背上抱着唐小虾开始害怕起来，她有点想让前面的人慢点，可人家毕竟急着去救人，她张了张嘴，却也没好意思说出来。害怕的时间久了，当害怕变成习惯，洛思琦慢慢睁开了刚才因加快速度而禁闭的眼睛，尽管四周的景色还是在不断的变换，马跑出来的风也有一些，可再快也快不到现在的汽车，时间长了，唐小虾驾着马也没出什么问题，洛思琪的心也渐渐的放下了。中午的时候在一个小镇匆匆的吃了饭，大家便就又开始上路，这样的长时间骑马让洛思琪不太好受，不过伍绪说很快就要到康城了，到康城可以给她找一辆马车，这让洛思琪很期待，便也坚持着跟大部队一起走了。伍绪说的很快让洛思琪很无语，很快，很快，却怎么也不到，好不容易到了天快黑的时候，他们才见到了那座叫做康城的小城，小城里的客栈不多，伍绪为他们选了一家最好的，客栈的名字叫永宁。洛思琪从马上下来觉得两条腿都要快站不住了，唐小虾却还有心情站在客栈的牌匾下说：“永宁，永宁，永远安宁，这个名字起的好啊！”身后的洛思琪恨不得一脚把他从门外踹进去，但她已经没有这个力气了，只有催促他快进去，说自己快要累死了。这间客栈还算比较大，分上下两层，洛思琦从小到大还是第一次住客栈，看什么都觉得新鲜，说是两层，其实楼下和饭馆并没有差太多，有一些穿着各异的人分散在几张桌子上吃饭，不过再新鲜，洛思琦也没有心思细看，她已经骑马骑了整整一天了，她要赶紧找一个房间好好的休息一下，累的不行的她连饭现在都没胃口吃。开房的时候伍家的人居然还问唐小虾要和洛思琦住一间还是两间，洛思琦赶紧说两间，说完之后自己都觉得面皮发烫红了脸，可唐小虾却说：“还是一间吧，师妹第一次出门，这样照顾起来也方便。”洛思琪十分坚决的给拒绝了，她很恼怒的看着唐小虾，心想这家伙这些天来一直不错，怎么突然露出色狼野心来了！唐小虾见她这么坚决也不再坚持，自顾自的回房间休息去了，倒是洛思琪纳闷了老半天，心想唐小虾突然间到底怎么了！", "source": "www.quanwenyuedu.io", "source_url": "https://www.quanwenyuedu.io/n/laidaochunqiudangyueshen/9.html", "_fixed": true, "content_en": "Chapter 8 Inexplicable Request Qing Yuanzi did not expect that Tang Xiaoxia would make this request. He was stunned for a moment, then smiled: \"I saw that you have been practicing swordsmanship diligently recently, and I thought you would ask me for a good sword. I have a Lingyun Sword, which is extraordinary. I will give it to you for self-defense.\" After saying that, he opened a box next to the table. There were two swords in the box, one with a sky blue scabbard, which is the Lingyun Sword. The scabbard of the other sword is silver-white, and the blade is slightly shorter, but it is the snow-covered sword that Qing Yuanzi wants to give to Luo Siqi. Qing Yuanzi explained that he also found these two swords in the cave based on the ancient secret scrolls. Now he only knows that they are sharp, but he does not know whether they have special abilities. He also took out two small cloth bags from a small box on the table and handed them to Tang Xiaoxia and Luo Siqi respectively: \"Inside are some gold coins and silver cloth coins. Although you haven't come out of the valley, I have told you the approximate value of these money before. Without further ado, you should get on your way! The Wu family is waiting for you at the entrance of the valley.\" Luo Siqi took a small cloth bag from Qing Yuanzi. Although the small cloth bag was not big, it was very heavy. When she thought that it was filled with gold and silver, Luo Siqi felt that her whole body was full of security. At least she would not starve to death in this era! When she thought of this, the more she looked at Tang Xiaoxia, the more she liked him. She wondered whether this handsome guy was smart or a money-crazy guy. In such a special and rushed environment, he actually thought of making some money first! On the other side, after collecting the money, Tang Xiaoxia slowly pulled out the Lingyun Sword. The Lingyun Sword glowed slightly with blue light after it was unsheathed. At first glance, it was not comparable to the ordinary sword on Wu Xu's waist. The blade of Luo Siqi's snow-covered sword was silver-white like the scabbard. The silver-white light made her feel a little cold, so she quickly inserted the sword back. Qing Yuanzi sent the two of them to the Wu family who were waiting outside. The junior brother had already ordered the maids to pack the other things they wanted to use in their luggage. Luo Siqi didn't know what the junior brother had packed for her in the luggage, but Luo Siqi felt that it didn't matter! She didn’t know what she was going to pack anyway! Wu Xu saluted them and did not introduce anyone else in the Wu family. He said to Tang Xiaoxia and Luo Siqi: \"The situation is urgent. Please come with me!\" Wu Xu was about the same height as Tang Xiaoxia and was about thirty years old. Luo Siqi had no time to think about him and instead went to see the two horses brought by his junior brother. The horses that the junior brother brought looked good, but this was a problem for Luo Siqi. Luo Siqi, who comes from modern society, can't ride a horse at all! Luo Siqi looked at Tang Xiaoxia and saw that he also had a solemn expression, but he still walked up to a big red horse, stepped on the mounting stone, turned over and rode on it. Luo Siqi almost fell down after seeing him get on the horse, but she still grabbed the horse's mane and pretended to be calm. His face looked very pale, but he still smiled and shouted to Luo Siqi: \"Junior sister, come up! Ride on the same horse with senior brother!\" Looking at the stepping stone that Tang Xiaoxia had just stepped on, Luo Siqi sat down behind Tang Xiaoxia. This was Luo Siqi's first time riding a real horse, and she was a little scared. But she was too embarrassed to hug Tang Xiaoxia's waist. She even felt that Tang Xiaoxia couldn't protect himself. She was afraid that if Ma really started running, hugging him would only cause the two of them to fall to the ground. Because there were people from the Wu family present, Tang Xiaoxia did not say to Qing Yuanzi: \"Old man! Goodbye!\" Instead, he said, \"Master, let's go!\", and then he patted his horse and followed the Wu family. The horse was bumpy when it started running. In order not to fall off, Luo Siqi had no choice but to feel embarrassed. She gently hugged Tang Xiaoxia's waist. Tang Xiaoxia reacted to her hug. He lowered his body slightly and grabbed the horse tightly, so that the two of them did not fall instantly. Because the road out of the valley had many twists and turns and was rugged, the two of them rode at a slow speed. When Luo Siqi gradually got used to the feeling of being on horseback, the two of them followed the Wu family's horse team and almost left the valley. At this time, Luo Siqi suddenly remembered that she and Tang Xiaoxia had lived in the valley for many days and actually forgot to ask Qing Yuanzi the name of the valley. She told Tang Xiaoxia about this, and Tang Xiaoxia smiled sheepishly and said, \"I forgot too!\" But when they arrived at the entrance of the valley, the two of them saw three black characters painted with ink on a cliff on the left. Luo Siqi couldn't help laughing and said: \"The name of this valley is really funny. Flowers are blooming everywhere in this valley, and there are green grasses. How could it have anything to do with snow! I think it should be called Baihua Valley!\" Tang Xiaoxia also agreed with Luo Siqi's statement. He said while driving his horse, \"Yes! The name Xueyun Valley sounds like a canyon in a high-altitude mountain range like Kunlun Mountain. This place If we are in Chu State, it should be in the middle and lower reaches of the Yangtze River. It is too difficult for snow here!\" After leaving the valley, the Wu family's horse team in front began to speed up. Luo Siqi started to get scared while holding Tang Xiaoxia on the horseback. She wanted the people in front to slow down, but after all, they were in a hurry to save people. She opened her mouth, but she was too embarrassed to say it. After being afraid for a long time, when fear became a habit, Luo Siqi slowly opened the eyes that had been closed due to speeding up. Although the surrounding scenery was still changing, and the horse ran out of the wind, there was some wind, but no matter how fast it was, it was not as fast as the current car. As time went by, Tang Xiaoxia drove the horse without any problems, and Luo Siqi gradually relaxed. After a quick meal in a small town at noon, everyone started on the road again. Such a long ride made Luo Siqi feel uncomfortable. However, Wu Xu said that they would arrive in Cannes soon, and they could find her a carriage when they arrived in Cannes. This made Luo Siqi look forward to it, so she insisted on going with the group. Wu Xu spoke very quickly, leaving Luo Siqi speechless. Very quickly, very quickly, but never arrived. It was almost dark when he finally arrived.", "title_en": "Chapter 9"}